        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 4672,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 1837,
        "paragraph_id": "4F3CF5D6",
        "text": "By multiplying the volume balance by u, subtracting it from the momentum balance and dividing the result by V (Acell, hum) we arrive at the following equation:"
      }
    ],
    "following_nonempty_paragraphs": [
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 94766,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 4676,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 1841,
        "paragraph_id": "6A1DC1F4",
        "text": "Where Acell is the cell area and hum is the average depth of the cell around the u-point. The procedure for the second term (the others are straightforward) now boils down to integrating (only) the incoming fluxes over the interfaces and multiplying them with the difference between u in the cell and the component of velocity in the same direction at the upwind cell."
      },
      {
        "container_path": "models/XBeach/raw/source_code/trunk/doc/manual/XBeach_manual_kingsday.docx",
        "member": "word/document.xml",
        "start_xml_ordinal": 94878,
        "body_paragraph_zero_based": 4678,
        "direct_body_paragraph_zero_based": 1843,
        "paragraph_id": "1F2E8BBB",
        "text": "Figure 5.2 \t\t\tControl volume u-momentum balance and definition of fluxes"
      }
    ],
